TEXT -728 8 Left 5 ;A three-phase generator rated 400 MVA, 20k, 1500 rpm \nis connected to a 400 kV, 2000 MVA network through a \nDelta-Wye 400 MVA transformer. The turbine outputs 150MW\nactive power constantly to the synchronous machine.\nThe power feeds the two loads (sum of 30MW) and the \nrest (120MW) is fed into the voltage source \nAt t = 4s, a three-phase to ground fault occurs on the 400 kV\nbus. The fault is cleared after 10 cycles (t = 4.2 s).\nNOTE: The simulation output starts just at 3sec so the steady\nstate of the generator is reached before the fault occur
TEXT -1304 -248 Left 2 !.options vntol=10 abstol=100m reltol=0.005 trtol=1\n.param Rgnd=1e6\n.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
TEXT -1304 -208 Left 2 !.tran 0 10 3 0.1m
TEXT -984 -248 Left 2 !vst stufe 0 pwl 0s 1v
